    "explanation": "**[풀이]**\n\n주어진 조건: $\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\theta\\right)=-\\frac{1}{5}$\n\n**Step 1: $\\cos\\theta$ 구하기**\n\n삼각함수 덧셈공식을 이용하면:\n$$\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\theta\\right) = -\\sin\\theta = -\\frac{1}{5}$$\n\n따라서 $\\sin\\theta = \\frac{1}{5}$\n\n**Step 2: $\\cos\\theta$ 구하기**\n\n기본 항등식 $\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$을 이용:\n$$\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^2 + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$$\n$$\\frac{1}{25} + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$$\n$$\\cos^2\\theta = \\frac{24}{25}$$\n$$\\cos\\theta = \\pm\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{5}$$\n\n**Step 3: 주어진 식 정리하기**\n\n$$\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1-\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta} = \\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}$$\n\n(단, $\\sin\\theta \\neq 0$)\n\n$$= \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{5}} = 5$$\n\n**검증:**\n\n분모를 다시 확인하면 $1-\\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta = \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{25}$\n\n따라서:\n$$\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1-\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{5}}{\\frac{1}{25}} = \\frac{1}{5} \\times 25 = 5$$\n\n답: $\\boxed{5}$",
    "problem": "$\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\theta\\right)=-\\frac{1}{5}$일 때, $\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1-\\cos^2\\theta}$의 값은? [3점]\n\n① $-5$\n② $-\\sqrt{5}$\n③ $0$\n④ $\\sqrt{5}$\n⑤ $5$"
