    "explanation": "**[풀이]**\n\n주어진 함수는 $f(x) = \\frac{\\ln x}{x^2}$입니다.\n\n극한값 $\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(e+h)-f(e-2h)}{h}$을 구해야 합니다.\n\n**Step 1: 극한의 변형**\n\n$$\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(e+h)-f(e-2h)}{h} = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(e+h)-f(e)+f(e)-f(e-2h)}{h}$$\n\n**Step 2: 극한 분리**\n\n$$= \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(e+h)-f(e)}{h} + \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(e)-f(e-2h)}{h}$$\n\n첫 번째 극한:\n$$\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(e+h)-f(e)}{h} = f'(e)$$\n\n두 번째 극한: $h \\to 0$일 때, $-2h \\to 0$이므로\n$$\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(e)-f(e-2h)}{h} = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(e-2h)-f(e)}{-h} = 2f'(e)$$\n\n따라서 전체 극한값은 $f'(e) + 2f'(e) = 3f'(e)$\n\n**Step 3: $f'(x)$ 계산**\n\n$$f'(x) = \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{x^2}\\right)$$\n\n몫의 미분법을 적용하면:\n$$f'(x) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{x} \\cdot x^2 - \\ln x \\cdot 2x}{x^4} = \\frac{x - 2x\\ln x}{x^4} = \\frac{1-2\\ln x}{x^3}$$\n\n**Step 4: $f'(e)$ 계산**\n\n$$f'(e) = \\frac{1-2\\ln e}{e^3} = \\frac{1-2 \\cdot 1}{e^3} = \\frac{-1}{e^3}$$\n\n**Step 5: 최종 답**\n\n$$3f'(e) = 3 \\cdot \\frac{-1}{e^3} = -\\frac{3}{e^3}$$",
    "problem": "함수 $f(x) = \\frac{\\ln x}{x^2}$에 대하여 $\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(e+h)-f(e-2h)}{h}$의 값은?\n\n① $-\\frac{2}{e}$\n\n② $-\\frac{3}{e^2}$\n\n③ $-\\frac{1}{e}$\n\n④ $-\\frac{2}{e^2}$\n\n⑤ $-\\frac{3}{e^3}$"
