    "explanation": "**[풀이]**\n\n주어진 적분: $\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}} x^3 \\sqrt{x^2-1} dx$\n\n**Step 1: 치환**\n\n$u = x^2 - 1$로 놓으면:\n- $du = 2x dx$\n- $x^2 = u + 1$\n- $x dx = \\frac{1}{2}du$\n\n적분 구간:\n- $x = 1$일 때: $u = 0$\n- $x = \\sqrt{2}$일 때: $u = 1$\n\n**Step 2: 적분 변환**\n\n$x^3 \\sqrt{x^2-1} dx = x^2 \\cdot \\sqrt{x^2-1} \\cdot x dx$\n\n$= (u+1) \\sqrt{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du$\n\n$= \\frac{1}{2}(u+1)u^{1/2} du$\n\n$= \\frac{1}{2}(u^{3/2} + u^{1/2}) du$\n\n**Step 3: 부정적분**\n\n$\\int \\frac{1}{2}(u^{3/2} + u^{1/2}) du = \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\frac{2}{5}u^{5/2} + \\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\right]$\n\n$= \\frac{1}{5}u^{5/2} + \\frac{1}{3}u^{3/2}$\n\n**Step 4: 정적분 계산**\n\n$\\left[\\frac{1}{5}u^{5/2} + \\frac{1}{3}u^{3/2}\\right]_0^1$\n\n$= \\left(\\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 0$\n\n$= \\frac{3}{15} + \\frac{5}{15}$\n\n$= \\frac{8}{15}$\n\n따라서 답은 $\\boxed{\\frac{8}{15}}$",
    "problem": "$\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}} x^3\\sqrt{x^2-1} dx$의 값은? [3점]\n\n① $\\frac{7}{15}$\n\n② $\\frac{8}{15}$\n\n③ $\\frac{3}{5}$\n\n④ $\\frac{2}{3}$\n\n⑤ $\\frac{11}{15}$"
