    "explanation": "**[풀이]**\n\n주어진 방정식: $2\\sin^2 x + 3\\cos x = 3$ (단, $0 \\le x < 2\\pi$)\n\n**Step 1: $\\sin^2 x$를 $\\cos x$로 치환**\n\n$\\sin^2 x = 1 - \\cos^2 x$이므로:\n$$2(1-\\cos^2 x) + 3\\cos x = 3$$\n$$2 - 2\\cos^2 x + 3\\cos x = 3$$\n$$-2\\cos^2 x + 3\\cos x - 1 = 0$$\n$$2\\cos^2 x - 3\\cos x + 1 = 0$$\n\n**Step 2: 이차방정식 풀이**\n\n$t = \\cos x$로 놓으면:\n$$2t^2 - 3t + 1 = 0$$\n$$(2t-1)(t-1) = 0$$\n\n따라서 $t = \\frac{1}{2}$ 또는 $t = 1$\n\n**Step 3: $\\cos x = \\frac{1}{2}$ 풀이**\n\n$0 \\le x < 2\\pi$ 범위에서:\n$$x = \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\text{ 또는 } x = \\frac{5\\pi}{3}$$\n\n**Step 4: $\\cos x = 1$ 풀이**\n\n$0 \\le x < 2\\pi$ 범위에서:\n$$x = 0$$\n\n**Step 5: 검증**\n- $x = 0$: $2\\sin^2 0 + 3\\cos 0 = 0 + 3 = 3$ ✓\n- $x = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$: $2 \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})^2 + 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{3}{2} = 3$ ✓\n- $x = \\frac{5\\pi}{3}$: $2 \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})^2 + 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{3}{2} = 3$ ✓\n\n모든 해의 합: $0 + \\frac{\\pi}{3} + \\frac{5\\pi}{3} = 2\\pi$\n\n따라서 정답은 **②번 $\\pi$**입니다.",
    "problem": "$0 \\leq x < 2\\pi$일 때, 방정식\n\n$$2\\sin^2x + 3\\cos x = 3$$\n\n의 모든 해의 합은? [3점]\n\n① $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n\n② $\\pi$\n\n③ $\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$\n\n④ $2\\pi$\n\n⑤ $\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$"
